From 4e3d82f69a64cbe6a4dd9a86b348c756313c7b51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominikos Pritis <idominikos@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 22:59:27 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] ALSA: usb-audio: Add Audient iD24 mixer map

The Audient iD24 (2708:000d) has the same AudioControl topology as the
iD14: FEATURE_UNIT 12 advertises Volume on 4 of the 6 channels of
MIXER_UNIT 60, sits on the monitor mixer branch and is traced through to
the Speaker output terminal, so it is exported as "Speaker Playback
Volume" and userspace takes it for the stream master.  Apply the same
rename to "Monitor Mix Playback Volume" as commit 9c0564fcc21a ("ALSA:
usb-audio: Rename the Audient iD14 monitor mix volume control").

MIXER_UNIT 60's descriptor is malformed: bmMixerControls is all-ones
with 11 bytes of trailing junk and iMixer is 255 (lsusb prints "Junk at
end of descriptor").  The generic parser turns that into a fully
programmable 16x6 matrix and creates sixteen 6-channel "ADAT-8 Volume"
controls, named after a channel-name string.  The device ACKs SET_CUR on
them with the UAC2 (ICN << 8 | OCN) addressing, but nothing documents
what the cells mean, and alsactl restore rewrites all 96 of them to
-127 dB on every boot and hot-plug.  Ignore the unit.

FEATURE_UNIT 11 stalls GET_RANGE for its Input Gain control (control
11), so the driver falls back to a 0..1 placeholder range and logs
"11:0: cannot get min/max values for control 11 (id 11)" on every
plug and on every read of the control.  Ignore that control; the Phase
Inverter control on the same unit works and stays.

Tested on an iD24 (bcdDevice 1.12) on 7.3-rc1: the card now exposes
Monitor Mix Playback Volume, the ADAT-8 controls and the Input Gain
placeholder are gone, alsactl store succeeds, and the min/max message
no longer appears.
---
 sound/usb/mixer_maps.c | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/usb/mixer_maps.c b/sound/usb/mixer_maps.c
index ace4cca..9b76b3f 100644
--- a/sound/usb/mixer_maps.c
+++ b/sound/usb/mixer_maps.c
@@ -518,6 +518,24 @@ static const struct usbmix_name_map audient_id14_map[] = {
 	{}
 };
 
+/* Audient iD24: FU 12 has the same shape as on the iD14 -- Volume on 4 of
+ * the 6 channels of MIXER_UNIT 60, on the monitor mixer branch, traced to
+ * the Speaker terminal -- so it gets the same non-standard name for the
+ * same reason.  MIXER_UNIT 60 itself has a malformed descriptor (the
+ * bmMixerControls bitmap is all-ones with 11 bytes of trailing junk and
+ * iMixer is 255), so the generic parser turns it into a 16x6 matrix of
+ * "ADAT-8 Volume" controls named after a channel string; alsactl restore
+ * rewrites all 96 cells to -127 dB at every boot and hot-plug.  FU 11
+ * stalls GET_RANGE for Input Gain, which leaves a 0..1 placeholder range
+ * and logs "cannot get min/max values" on every read.  Drop both.
+ */
+static const struct usbmix_name_map audient_id24_map[] = {
+	{ 11, NULL, 11 },		/* FU, Input Gain: GET_RANGE stalls */
+	{ 12, "Monitor Mix Playback" },	/* FU, partial coverage */
+	{ 60, NULL },			/* MU, malformed descriptor */
+	{}
+};
+
 /*
  * Control map entries
  */
@@ -611,6 +629,11 @@ static const struct usbmix_ctl_map usbmix_ctl_maps[] = {
 		.id = USB_ID(0x2708, 0x0008),
 		.map = audient_id14_map,
 	},
+	{
+		/* Audient iD24 */
+		.id = USB_ID(0x2708, 0x000d),
+		.map = audient_id24_map,
+	},
 	{
 		/* KEF X300A */
 		.id = USB_ID(0x27ac, 0x1000),
-- 
2.55.0

